SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] running — 10km @ 6:45–7:00/km (67–70 min)\, wal
 k-run format if needed\; 
DESCRIPTION:10km @ 6:45–7:00/km (67–70 min)\, walk-run format if needed
 \; gate unchanged (body battery ≥55\, avg sleep ≥6.5h Aug 2–8) — d
 o not extend beyond 10km this week regardless of how good you feel.\n\nRea
 son: With the Treviso 10K 64 days away\, building run volume progressively
  from a low base is safer than jumping to 12km in the first real long run 
 after a recovery week — arriving at 10km comfortably is the goal here.\n
 \nAI coaching 2026-07-31
END:VEVENT
